.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt RUSTC 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm rustc
.Nd Rust compiler with the RavenBSD target
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm rustc
.Op + Ns Ar toolchain
.Op Fl -target Ar triple
.Op Ar options
.Ar input
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This page documents the patched stable Rust compiler installed by
.Pa make toolchain .
It is the upstream Rust compiler built from the pinned stable source release
with the reviewed RavenBSD target patch series; the language and existing
targets are unchanged.
.Pp
The patched compiler is registered with
.Xr rustup 1
as the custom toolchain
.Dq ravenbsd
and lives in
.Pa build/toolchain .
Select it explicitly:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rustc +ravenbsd --version
rustc +ravenbsd --target x86_64-unknown-ravenbsd --emit=metadata crate.rs
.Ed
.Pp
The target triples added by the patch series are
.Dq x86_64-unknown-ravenbsd ,
.Dq aarch64-unknown-ravenbsd
and
.Dq riscv64gc-unknown-ravenbsd .
Only
.Dq x86_64-unknown-ravenbsd
is verified by the K19 gate; the other two are draft target specs.
The target is static-only
.Pq Va dynamic_linking No = false ,
uses the
.Dq relibc
environment and
.Dq rust-lld
as its linker.
Standard library support for the target is a later gate
.Pq K20 Ns / Ns K22 ;
the K19 acceptance compiles metadata only.
.Pp
The source release and the SHA-256 of the source tarball are recorded in
.Pa toolchain/rust-version .
The script downloads the tarball once, verifies the hash, applies
.Pa toolchain/patches/*.patch
and reuses the verified source and install on later runs.
It fails rather than falling back to a different release, a nightly compiler
or an unverified archive.
.Pp
The default stage is 1. A stage-2 compiler can be built with
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make toolchain TOOLCHAIN_STAGE=2
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width build/toolchain-src -compact
.It Pa build/toolchain
installed custom toolchain
.It Pa build/toolchain-src
patched Rust source and incremental bootstrap build tree
.It Pa toolchain/rust-version
pinned release and source hash
.It Pa toolchain/bootstrap.toml
host and RavenBSD target bootstrap configuration
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cargo 1 ,
.Xr rustup 1
.Sh STANDARDS
Rust 1.97.1 stable, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
